			"Message": "docs(Common): Restructure README with expanded sections and directory tree\n\nOverhaul the Common crate README to improve scannability, add comprehensive\nproject documentation, and align with the updated documentation hosting domain.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Add em-quad spacing and landscape emoji to the title heading for consistent\n  project-wide README styling\n- Replace the verbose welcome paragraph with a concise \"Key Features\" section\n  that explains the ActionEffect system, compile-time DI, DTO library, unified\n  error handling, transport layer, and telemetry pipe with proper technical depth\n- Relocate the Core Architecture Principles table earlier in the document,\n  positioning it before the System Architecture diagram for logical flow\n- Replace the standalone ActionEffect code example with an expanded in-situ\n  explanation under Key Features, then move the full runnable example to a\n  dedicated section after the architecture content\n- Add a full Project Structure directory tree listing every Source/ subdirectory\n  to serve as a browsable crate map for new contributors\n- Introduce a dependency flow table mapping each consumer (Mountain, Grove, Air,\n  Sidecars, Tests, Cocoon) to their relationship with Common\n- Add a Security section detailing layer-by-layer architectural guarantees\n  (type system, error model, dependencies, data contracts)\n- Add a Compatibility section enumerating all integration targets and their\n  role in the Land ecosystem\n- Update the API documentation link to the new dedicated subdomain pattern\n\nThe restructured README now serves as both a project overview and a developer\nonboarding guide, reducing time to first contribution.",
